      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You should look at indicators like average income levels in the zip code, which often correlate with neighborhood stability. Also, crime rates and the percentage of long-term residents can serve as proxies for community cohesion. These socioeconomic factors provide a much richer picture than just credit history alone.",
