      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The best way to fine-tune this is to focus on the *rate of change* in these indicators, rather than the raw values. For example, a rapidly declining average income or a sudden spike in crime suggests instability, regardless of who lives there. Furthermore, look at local business turnover rates; a stable local economy is a better predictor of reliability than any demographic proxy.",
      "source": "target",
